{"name":"Vice City","hex":"#ee00dd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Bad or immoral behavior. (Especially often, a habit that harms oneself or others)","Any of various crimes related (depending on jurisdiction) to weapons, prostitution, pornography, gambling, alcohol, tobacco, or drugs."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of vise (“mechanical screw apparatus used for clamping”).","A tool for drawing lead into cames, or flat grooved rods, for casements."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vice"},{"term":"city","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large settlement, bigger than a town; sometimes with a specific legal definition, depending on the place.","A settlement granted special status by royal charter or letters patent; traditionally, a settlement with a cathedral regardless of size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vice City (XXXTentacion song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Vice City\" is a song by American rapper and singer XXXTentacion. It was originally released on SoundCloud on March 5, 2014, before being re-released posthumously for streaming services on January 28, 2022. The song was produced by Canis Major and heavily samples the 2013 song \"Sing to the Moon\" by British soul artist Laura Mvula."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/XXXTentacion_-_Vice_City.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vice_City_(XXXTentacion_song)","wikidata":"Q110724266"},{"title":"Vice City (Jay Rock song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Vice City\" is a song by American rapper Jay Rock, taken from his second studio album, 90059. The song, which was produced by Cardo and Yung Exclusive, features guest appearances from Rock's fellow TDE label-mates Kendrick Lamar, Schoolboy Q and Ab-Soul, credited as they are collectively known, Black Hippy. The song takes its name from the 2002 video game Grand Theft Auto: Vice City."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vice_City_(Jay_Rock_song)","wikidata":"Q20967722"},{"title":"Grand Theft Auto: Vice City","blocks":[{"text":"Grand Theft Auto: Vice City is a 2002 action-adventure game developed by Rockstar North and published by Rockstar Games. It is the fourth main game in the Grand Theft Auto series, following 2001's Grand Theft Auto III, and the sixth entry overall. Set in 1986 within the fictional Vice City, the single-player story follows gangster Tommy Vercetti's rise to power after being released from prison and becoming caught up in an ambushed drug deal. While seeking out those responsible, Tommy gradually builds a criminal empire by seizing power from other criminal organisations."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ce/Vice-city-cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Theft_Auto%3A_Vice_City","wikidata":"Q94671"},{"title":"Vice","blocks":[{"text":"A vice is a practice, behaviour, habit or item generally considered morally wrong in the associated society. In more minor usage, vice can refer to a fault, a negative character trait, a defect, an infirmity, or a bad or unhealthy habit. Vices are usually associated with a fault in a person's character or temperament rather than their morality."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Die_Tugend_ruft_die_Jugend_zur%C3%BCck_%28aus_den_Armen_der_S%C3%BCnde%29%2C_1806-1807_-_Johann_Heinrich_F%C3%BCssli.jpg/330px-Die_Tugend_ruft_die_Jugend_zur%C3%BCck_%28aus_den_Armen_der_S%C3%BCnde%29%2C_1806-1807_-_Johann_Heinrich_F%C3%BCssli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vice","wikidata":"Q1411242"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c5/Grand_Theft_Auto_Vice_City_moto